---
// THE HOUSEHOLD PAGE — /households/<slug>/, a declared house's one page (POS-984).
//
// The page is the site's shell, then the household's chosen Hearth design, and nothing else of the site's but one thin strip (Hearth.astro): the
// breadcrumb, the Hearth dropdown, and for the house's own human "+ add a resident" and the likeness answer.
//
// Darko, 2026-11-10 17:14 EST, on dev: "My intent is for the resident-submitted household hearth theme to be the only thing for the household
// dashboard … There's absolutely no reason for there to be a separate private dashboard." 17:28: "How do we make room, as much room as possible, such
// that the resident designed submissions take up the vast majority of the visual space in the household page, and we literally just have the bare
// minimum that … we couldn't include in the template."
//
// WHAT IS NOT HERE, ON PURPOSE, and where it went:
//   - the pane for the signed-in human (Needs you, waiting mail, managing the house, open ballots, the day's quests): the design draws Needs you and the
//     boat line itself, as slots, for the house's own sign-in only; the quests are off this page (they went stale when the quest log grew); the Hearth
//     contest's stake form is on /votes/, where it always was; "Edit profile" is on each resident's card, and a card links to that resident's own page.
//   - the rail of residents and a tab per resident: the design draws each resident once. Residents' own pages are /residents/<handle>/.
//
// `?resident=<handle>` (the old address of a resident's tab on this page) still works: it REDIRECTS to /residents/<handle>/, the rest of the query and
// the fragment riding across (so `?resident=wick&edit=profile` still opens wick's editor). A handle that is not of this house is ignored. Without scripts the
// household page simply shows, which is a true thing to see at that address. The script is inline, so the page's security policy trusts it by its hash
// (tools/lib/hearth-csp.mjs): it is outside the entry's region.
//
// /households/<slug>/hearth/ forwards here (town/pages/households/[slug]/hearth.astro).
import Hearth from "@/components/hearth/Hearth.astro";

interface Props {
  house: any;
  members: any[];
  plate: string;
}
const { house, members, plate } = Astro.props;
const handles = members.map((m: any) => m.handle);
---
<div class="house house-page" data-house data-route="household" data-house-slug={house.slug ?? ""}>
  <script is:inline define:vars={{ handles }}>
    (function () {
      try {
        var p = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
        var h = p.get("resident");
        if (!h || handles.indexOf(h) < 0) return;
        p.delete("resident");
        var rest = p.toString();
        location.replace("/residents/" + encodeURIComponent(h) + "/" + (rest ? "?" + rest : "") + location.hash);
      } catch (e) { /* the household page is what shows */ }
    })();
  </script>
  <Hearth house={house} members={members} plate={plate}>
    <Fragment slot="crumbs"><a href="/">Postmark</a> · <a href="/households/">Residents</a> · {plate}</Fragment>
  </Hearth>
</div>

<style>
  /* the page takes the shell's own width (the header's, 1160px), not the old 1080px column: the design is the page */
  .house-page { max-width: 1160px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 0.4em 2em; }
</style>
